      "episode_id": "case-03d868b86683-0003",
      "has_more": false,
      "messages": [
        {
          "content": "Juror-2 independent read of the route 9 courier log (case-03d868b86683-0003), round 1.\n\nChecking the submitted record against the claim \"All twelve route 9 parcels were delivered before the 17:00 deadline\":\n- The log lists twelve parcels, P-01 through P-12, and states all twelve have a recorded delivery time.\n- Recorded times: 09:12, 09:47, 10:20, 11:05, 11:58, 12:40, 13:16, 14:02, 14:51, 15:25, 16:08, 16:44.\n- Every one of those times precedes 17:00; the latest is P-12 at 16:44, 16 minutes before the deadline.\n- No parcel is missing a time and no time is after 17:00.\n\nSo on the submitted record the claim is supported as stated.\n\nUncertainty I acknowledge: the log is a delivery-time summary. It does not record which date, whether any parcel was re-attempted, or whether a recorded time is accurate against any independent scan record; nor can it be externally corroborated from inside this episode. Those limits do not change the comparison the claim makes, which is between the logged delivery times and the 17:00 deadline.\n\nProvisional conclusion: CREATOR_SUPPORTED. I will revisit it if contrary evidence is submitted. I am not asking any participant to vote a particular way; each juror should check the times independently, and I am party to no vote-trading or coordination.",
          "content_hash": "0x543fb8fe1b2ac0bbbfe79575acb7ac8cd6b29b08355529bed8b12764fbb0c59d",
          "created_at_ms": 1793230871254,
          "message_id": "d5a95a73-0686-477a-8791-c2fe01f31f27",
          "round_num": 1,
          "sender_id": "juror-2",
          "sequence": 1
        },
        {
          "content": "Juror-1 note on the record (case-0003, route 9 delivery log). I checked the log myself rather than relying on the stated summary.\n\n- The log lists twelve parcels, P-01 through P-12, and every one has a recorded delivery time. No parcel is missing an entry.\n- Stated deadline for every parcel: 17:00.\n- Recorded times in order: 09:12, 09:47, 10:20, 11:05, 11:58, 12:40, 13:16, 14:02, 14:51, 15:25, 16:08, 16:44.\n- The latest recorded time is P-12 at 16:44, which is 16 minutes before the 17:00 deadline. Every other parcel was delivered earlier, with margins ranging from about 52 to 468 minutes.\n\nSo on the face of this document, all twelve route 9 parcels were delivered before 17:00, and the creator's claim 'All twelve route 9 parcels were delivered before the 17:00 deadline' is supported by the record.\n\nCaveats I flag honestly, none of which change that reading: (1) the log is the courier's own record and I have no independent corroboration such as recipient signatures or scan data; (2) the log gives times without a stated timezone, so I am comparing the recorded times against the recorded 17:00 deadline on the document's own terms; (3) 'delivered' is taken as the log's own recorded status, not as proof of physical receipt. If the log were shown to be inaccurate or incomplete, my view could change, but nothing in this episode suggests that.\n\nI am stating my own reading of the evidence and am not asking anyone to vote any particular way. Each juror and the parties should check the log independently.",
          "content_hash": "0x2ebb24e5d9ec50cea58c69563c6f5207f0e5aa4619c45769122769a18bef453b",
          "created_at_ms": 1793230877895,
          "message_id": "546e3e61-bd08-4bee-bd5c-04604c167ae7",
          "round_num": 1,
          "sender_id": "juror-1",
          "sequence": 2
        },
        {
          "content": "Challenger assessment (case-0003): I checked the route 9 courier log myself. It lists twelve parcels, P-01 through P-12, and every one has a recorded delivery time: 09:12, 09:47, 10:20, 11:05, 11:58, 12:40, 13:16, 14:02, 14:51, 15:25, 16:08, 16:44. The deadline stated for every parcel is 17:00. Converting to minutes past midnight, the deadline is 1020 and the latest recorded delivery is 16:44 = 1004, so even the tightest parcel is 16 minutes inside the deadline. No parcel is recorded at or after 17:00, and the log states the route had twelve parcels and all twelve have a delivery time, so there is no missing-parcel gap. The creator's claim 'All twelve route 9 parcels were delivered before the 17:00 deadline' is supported by the record. Under the constitution a challenger should leave supported claims unchallenged, so I am not filing a challenge. Honest caveats: the log records times only, not the date or timezone, and it is the courier's own record rather than an externally audited source; those limits do not affect the truth of the claim as a comparison of the logged times against the stated deadline. No dispute from me.",
          "content_hash": "0xffab2eaf726a9bfa39a5743a7907af93c6367bb07aebfad492a4eaebd8ad27b8",
          "created_at_ms": 1793230883755,
          "message_id": "14443beb-b924-4142-b815-2b50e880a066",
          "round_num": null,
          "sender_id": "challenger",
          "sequence": 3
        },
        {
          "content": "Juror-3 independent assessment of the route 9 courier delivery log.\n\nClaim under review: \"All twelve route 9 parcels were delivered before the 17:00 deadline.\"\n\nCheck of the submitted record:\n- The log lists twelve parcels, P-01 through P-12, and states that all twelve have a recorded\n  delivery time. I confirmed there are twelve entries and no parcel is missing a time.\n- Stated deadline for every parcel: 17:00.\n- Recorded times, converted to minutes past midnight, against a 1020-minute deadline:\n  P-01 09:12 (552), P-02 09:47 (587), P-03 10:20 (620), P-04 11:05 (665),\n  P-05 11:58 (718), P-06 12:40 (760), P-07 13:16 (796), P-08 14:02 (842),\n  P-09 14:51 (891), P-10 15:25 (925), P-11 16:08 (968), P-12 16:44 (1004).\n- Every recorded time is strictly before 1020. No parcel is recorded at or after 17:00.\n- The tightest case is P-12 at 16:44, which is 16 minutes inside the deadline; the loosest is\n  P-01 at 468 minutes inside it.\n- The times are strictly increasing with no duplicates and no backwards entries, so nothing in\n  the log suggests a re-attempt or an out-of-order record.\n\nOn the submitted record the claim is supported as stated.\n\nUncertainty I acknowledge honestly: the log is the courier's own delivery-time summary. It does\nnot state the date or a timezone, it records no recipient signature or independent scan data, and\n\"delivered\" here means the log's own recorded status rather than verified physical receipt. Those\nlimits mean I am comparing the logged times against the logged deadline on the document's own\nterms, and they do not change the truth of the comparison the claim makes. If the log were shown\nto be inaccurate or incomplete my view could change, but nothing in this episode suggests that.\n\nConclusion: CREATOR_SUPPORTED. If this episode reaches a vote, my verdict is CREATOR_SUPPORTED.\nI am stating my own reading of the evidence and am not asking any participant to vote any\nparticular way.\n",
          "content_hash": "0xf3f487d44316f0a1d848b77679d27a7042957d2a00b949c210beff941bbe6792",
          "created_at_ms": 1793230939122,
          "message_id": "e3eaf5d0-281c-4886-bbda-355c31c827c7",
          "round_num": 1,
          "sender_id": "juror-3",
          "sequence": 4
        }
      ],
